  "enhanced_information": "Kinesins and dyneins are associated with microtubules, not intermediate filaments. Examples of intermediate filaments include keratin, desmin, and vimentin, providing structural support to the cell. Microtubules are indeed formed by polymerization of tubulin proteins and are dynamic structures involved in intracellular transport. Centrioles are formed by 9 microtubule triplets, not doublets, playing a role in organizing the microtubule network in the cell."
